The configuration of cairo and pixman for the Emscripten VM
===========================================================

cmake/emscripten/deps/cairo.cmake and pixman.cmake build cairo 1.18.4 and
pixman 0.44.2 with CMake alone, from their release archives: `make wasm'
needs no meson, ninja nor pkg-config.  What their meson builds would make at
configure time is committed instead, here and in ../pixman/:

    ../pixman/pixman-config.h      <pixman build>/pixman/pixman-config.h
    ../pixman/pixman-version.h     <pixman build>/pixman/pixman-version.h
    ../pixman/sources.cmake        the sources of <pixman build>'s
                                   libpixman-1.a
    config.h                       <cairo build>/config.h
    cairo-features.h               <cairo build>/src/cairo-features.h
    sources.cmake                  the sources of <cairo build>'s libcairo.a
    config-pdf.h                   <cairo PDF build>/config.h
    cairo-features-pdf.h           <cairo PDF build>/src/cairo-features.h
    sources-pdf.cmake              the sources that <cairo PDF build>'s
                                   libcairo.a has more

The headers are meson's output, unchanged but for two lines of config.h
and config-pdf.h (below).  The PDF configuration
(WASM_CAIRO_PDF) is cairo's with zlib: its PDF, PostScript and script
surfaces, which add CAIRO_HAS_PDF_SURFACE, CAIRO_HAS_PS_SURFACE and
CAIRO_HAS_SCRIPT_SURFACE to cairo-features.h, CAIRO_HAS_INTERPRETER and
HAVE_ZLIB to config.h, and four sources.  (That build also makes
libcairo-script-interpreter.a, which no image uses, and which is not built
here.)

They were made once, with meson 1.12.1 and ninja from pip, pkgconf from pip
as pkg-config, and emsdk 6.0.10, against Emscripten's ports of zlib 1.3.2,
libpng 1.6.58 and FreeType 2.14.3 (`embuilder build zlib libpng-wasmsjlj
freetype-wasmsjlj --wasm64', given to meson by .pc files of their own), in
the VM's mode: 64-bit objects and WebAssembly setjmp/longjmp.  The FreeType
the VM links is a leaner build of the same version
(cmake/emscripten/deps/freetype.cmake), whose headers and functions are the
same: what meson found of FreeType (HAVE_FT_COLR_V1, HAVE_FT_SVG_DOCUMENT,
HAVE_FT_LOAD_NO_SVG) holds for it too, and cairo.cmake stops the build
unless the FreeType headers are those of 2.14.3.

The two lines of config.h and config-pdf.h that differ from meson's comment
out HAVE_FT_COLR_V1 and HAVE_FT_SVG_DOCUMENT.  They turn on cairo's
renderers of COLR v1 and OT-SVG colour glyphs (cairo-colr-glyph-render.c,
cairo-svg-glyph-render.c), which the VM's FreeType never asks for: it is
built without TT_CONFIG_OPTION_COLOR_LAYERS (FT_Get_Color_Glyph_Paint finds
no paint) nor FT_CONFIG_OPTION_SVG (no glyph has FT_GLYPH_FORMAT_SVG).
Without them pharo-web.wasm is 47,913 bytes smaller (17,896 gzipped), and
draws the same.

The cross file:

    [binaries]
    c = 'emcc'
    cpp = 'em++'
    ar = 'emar'
    ranlib = 'emranlib'
    strip = 'emstrip'
    pkg-config = '<pkgconf>'
    [built-in options]
    c_args = ['-m64', '-sSUPPORT_LONGJMP=wasm', '-sWASM_LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS=0']
    c_link_args = ['-m64', '-sSUPPORT_LONGJMP=wasm', '-sWASM_LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS=0']
    [properties]
    needs_exe_wrapper = true
    pkg_config_libdir = ['<the .pc files of the ports>', '<prefix>/lib/pkgconfig']
    [host_machine]
    system = 'emscripten'
    cpu_family = 'wasm64'
    cpu = 'wasm64'
    endian = 'little'

pixman, without its threads dependency first (meson turns it into -pthread
on Emscripten, which makes the memory of the module shared, and would reach
every user of pixman-1.pc):

    sed -i "s/^dep_threads = dependency('threads')$/dep_threads = null_dep/" \
        pixman-0.44.2/meson.build
    meson setup <pixman build> pixman-0.44.2 --cross-file wasm64.cross \
        --prefix=<prefix> --default-library=static --buildtype=release \
        -Doptimization=2 -Dloongson-mmi=disabled -Dmmx=disabled \
        -Dsse2=disabled -Dssse3=disabled -Dvmx=disabled -Darm-simd=disabled \
        -Dneon=disabled -Da64-neon=disabled -Drvv=disabled \
        -Dmips-dspr2=disabled -Dgnu-inline-asm=disabled -Dopenmp=disabled \
        -Dtimers=false -Dgtk=disabled -Dlibpng=disabled -Dtests=disabled \
        -Ddemos=disabled
    ninja -C <pixman build> install

cairo, twice, with -Dzlib=disabled (<cairo build>) and -Dzlib=enabled
(<cairo PDF build>):

    meson setup <cairo build> cairo-1.18.4 --cross-file wasm64.cross \
        --prefix=<prefix> --default-library=static --buildtype=release \
        -Doptimization=2 -Ddwrite=disabled -Dfontconfig=disabled \
        -Dfreetype=enabled -Dpng=enabled -Dquartz=disabled -Dtee=disabled \
        -Dxcb=disabled -Dxlib=disabled -Dtests=disabled -Dlzo=disabled \
        -Dglib=disabled -Dspectre=disabled -Dsymbol-lookup=disabled \
        -Dzlib=disabled
    ninja -C <cairo build>

The source lists are the files of the build's compile_commands.json in the
archive's src/ (cairo) and pixman/ (pixman), that is

    python3 -c 'import json, os, sys
    for e in json.load(open(sys.argv[1])):
        f = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(e["directory"], e["file"]))
        if os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(f)) == sys.argv[2]:
            print(os.path.basename(f))' <cairo build>/compile_commands.json src | sort

(and <pixman build>/compile_commands.json pixman): cairo's build also
compiles boilerplate/ and util/, for its tests and tools.
The compile options of cairo.cmake and pixman.cmake are those of the same
compile commands, without their warnings, -fPIC and _FORTIFY_SOURCE: cairo
(-std=gnu11 -fno-strict-aliasing -fno-common -fvisibility=hidden,
CAIRO_COMPILATION, _REENTRANT, _GNU_SOURCE) and pixman (-std=gnu99
-fno-strict-aliasing -fvisibility=hidden -ftrapping-math, HAVE_CONFIG_H).

config.h also says what only cairo's tests and tools use (HAVE_FORK,
HAVE_WAITPID, HAVE_SYS_SOCKET_H...), as pixman-config.h does (HAVE_ALARM,
HAVE_SIGACTION).  CAIRO_HAS_PTHREAD and CAIRO_HAS_REAL_PTHREAD put cairo's
mutexes on pthread_mutex_*, which, without -pthread, are Emscripten's
single-thread stubs.

The CMake build of these files drew the same pixels as the meson build (a
C test of paths, gradients, FreeType text and PNG output in node).  They
must be made again, as above, for another version of cairo, pixman or
FreeType, or other options: cairo.cmake and pixman.cmake stop the build when
an archive is not of the version they were made for.
